/** \file programming.dox
 * \brief Introduction to the hciReduce Developer's Guide.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup programming_guide
 * @{
 *
 * This introduction explains how the principal hciReduce components fit together. The code-oriented
 * \ref developer_klip_algorithm "KLIP Algorithm" and \ref developer_p4_algorithm "P4 Algorithm" pages trace the
 * algorithm implementations in more detail. The public library API is collected under
 * \ref programming_library "Library API".
 *
 * \section programming_hierarchy Class hierarchy
 *
 * \code{.unparsed}
 * HCIobservation
 * └── ADIobservation
 *     ├── KLIPreduction
 *     └── P4Reduction
 * \endcode
 *
 * \ref mx::improc::HCIobservation "HCIobservation" owns input discovery, FITS I/O, optional coaddition and
 * preprocessing, common masks, final-image combination, and output. \ref mx::improc::ADIobservation
 * "ADIobservation" adds parallactic-angle derotation, fake-companion injection, and the shared final-processing
 * lifecycle. \ref mx::improc::KLIPreduction "KLIPreduction" supplies region-by-region KLIP PSF modeling, while
 * \ref mx::improc::P4Reduction "P4Reduction" supplies local pixel-prediction modeling.
 * \ref mx::improc::ADIDerotator "ADIDerotator" provides the standard configured image rotation transform.
 *
 * P4 further separates immutable geometry (\ref mx::improc::P4PixelGrid "P4PixelGrid") from the numerical
 * truncated-PCA calculation (\ref mx::improc::P4PCA "P4PCA"). That separation keeps geometry, numerical rank
 * handling, and reduction orchestration independently testable.
 *
 * \section programming_diagrams Documentation diagrams
 *
 * Standalone TikZ sources belong in `doc/figures` with a `.tex` extension. During `make docs`, CMake discovers
 * these sources and generates same-named PDF and SVG assets in the build tree whenever a source changes. Doxygen
 * copies both formats into the HTML output. Documentation pages can embed the SVG and link it to the PDF using the
 * shared file stem. If `latexmk` or `pdftocairo` is unavailable, the build uses same-named pre-rendered assets from
 * `doc/figures` and reports that fallback during configuration.
 *
 * \section programming_flow Execution flow
 *
 * Each application derives from `mx::app::application`, registers configuration targets, loads configuration, and
 * invokes its reduction object. A normal run proceeds from configuration to file discovery and FITS read, common
 * preprocessing, algorithm residuals, ADI final processing, and finally FITS products.
 *
 * Algorithms own their science-specific validation and provenance cards. The shared final-processing lifecycle owns
 * post-median subtraction, derotation, combination, validity materialization, and output gating so that algorithms
 * do not duplicate those stateful steps.
 *
 * \section programming_extension Extending hciReduce
 *
 * A new algorithm should reuse \ref mx::improc::HCIobservation "HCIobservation" or
 * \ref mx::improc::ADIobservation "ADIobservation" where their data and final-processing contracts fit, keep
 * non-trivial definitions in a `.cpp` file, expose documented configuration through `setupConfig` and `loadConfig`,
 * and add focused Catch2 tests. See \ref hcireduce_testing "Testing and Verification" for the build, coverage, and
 * documentation-link requirements.
 *
 * @}
 */
